Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 0/4] soundwire, ASoC, pinctrl: force runtime suspend across system sleep

The SoundWire controllers, WSA amplifiers, LPASS macros and LPI pin
controller only have runtime PM ops, so those an open stream holds
runtime-active stay up through system sleep and keep the SoC out of CX
power collapse. Each now forces its runtime suspend; the controllers,
amplifiers and macros skip it while a stream is still set up on them.
Based on the Armada project's patches.

